  "premise_review": [
    "Preserve C : Type u, [Category.{v} C] and arbitrary U : C. Cover stores k : Nat, object : Fin k → C and one arrow object i ⟶ U per index.",
    "k may be zero. No nonempty, jointly-surjective, jointly-epimorphic, topology-membership, refinement, base-change or transitivity condition is present.",
    "Index is exactly Fin S.k; length is exactly S.k. localObject and localArrow are direct projections with their original dependent index type.",
    "empty uses Fin0 elimination for both objects and arrows. identityCover has one copy of U with its identity arrow. Neither is asserted to be a covering family in an external topology.",
    "postcompose retains the same index size/object family and composes each arrow on the right with the supplied f : U ⟶ V. No functoriality or coverage-stability theorem is added.",
    "The only two theorems are rfl statements for the identity-family length and its local arrow, with both simp attributes retained exactly.",
    "All10 commands, universe/category context, dependent indices, constructor fields, equality statements and proof bodies are exact copies. Only enclosing namespaces and explicit same-version component imports change."
  ],
